CAT = "auforkliftPlan"; SEG = "PLN"
Q = [
("What does a site traffic management plan set out?",
 "Separating people and vehicles", ["Each truck's service intervals", "The load chart for every truck", "Which operators work overtime"],
 "A traffic management plan sets routes, crossings, speed limits, exclusion zones and how pedestrians and plant are separated. Follow the parts that apply to your role in the work area."),
("What is the purpose of an exclusion zone around a forklift task?",
 "Keeps people clear of the work", ["Stores the spare batteries", "Marks where loads are weighed", "Shows where trucks park overnight"],
 "An exclusion zone keeps pedestrians and other plant out of the area where the forklift and load could strike or crush them. Set it up before the lift starts."),
("A pedestrian walks into the aisle ahead of your loaded forklift. What should you do?",
 "Stop and wait till they're clear", ["Sound the horn and keep going", "Steer around them without slowing", "Flash the lights and continue"],
 "Stop and let the pedestrian clear the path before moving. A horn warns people but does not make it safe to drive at them."),
("You are approaching a blind intersection in a warehouse. What should you do?",
 "Slow down and sound the horn", ["Speed up to clear it quickly", "Keep your speed and use mirrors", "Flash the lights and keep going"],
 "Slow down, sound the horn and look before entering a blind corner or intersection. Mirrors help but are not enough on their own."),
("You must work near overhead power lines. What should you do first?",
 "Find the safe approach distance", ["Lift the mast to test clearance", "Work fast to cut exposure time", "Wear rubber-soled boots"],
 "Approach distances depend on the voltage and vary by state, so check them and plan the task, with a spotter if needed. Never test clearance with the mast, and boots give no real protection."),
("Before driving through a doorway, what must you check?",
 "Clearance for the mast and load", ["Width of the aisle and the forks", "Air pressure in the tyres", "Fuel level in the tank"],
 "Doorways, roof beams and sprinkler pipes can strike the mast or a raised load. Check the overhead clearance of the mast and load before going through."),
("The lighting in your work area has failed and you cannot see clearly. What should you do?",
 "Stop and get the lighting fixed", ["Rely on the truck's beeper", "Work faster to finish before dark", "Use the horn more often"],
 "Insufficient lighting is a hazard to identify and control before work continues. Stop, report it and use proper lighting before operating again."),
("You must use an LPG forklift in a poorly ventilated area. What is the main hazard?",
 "Carbon monoxide build-up", ["Hydrogen sulphide build-up", "Oxygen build-up", "Nitrogen build-up"],
 "Engine exhaust from LPG, petrol and diesel trucks contains carbon monoxide, which builds up in enclosed spaces. Hydrogen is the hazard when charging lead-acid batteries."),
("Strong gusts start while you are moving tall, light cartons outdoors. What is the safest action?",
 "Stop until the wind eases", ["Lift the load above the gusts", "Drive faster to finish the job", "Tilt the mast fully forward"],
 "Large, light loads act like a sail in wind and can tip the load or the truck. Stop, lower the load and wait for the wind to drop."),
("A lightning storm approaches while you are working in an open yard. What should you do?",
 "Stop work and take shelter", ["Keep working under the guard", "Raise the mast to earth it", "Keep going until it's overhead"],
 "Lightning is a serious hazard to anyone working outdoors on plant. Stop, park the truck safely and shelter until the storm passes."),
("The yard surface is wet or icy. How should you change the way you drive?",
 "Slow down and brake earlier", ["Drive normally; the tyres grip", "Brake harder and later", "Raise the load for weight"],
 "Water and ice cut tyre grip, so braking distances grow and the truck can slide. Drive slower, brake gently and allow more stopping distance."),
("On a very hot day of outdoor forklift work, how should you protect yourself?",
 "Drink water and take breaks", ["Remove your hi-vis vest", "Wear less PPE to stay cool", "Work through, rest at the end"],
 "Extreme heat causes heat stress and fatigue, which lead to mistakes. Drink water often and take rest breaks in the shade while keeping your PPE on."),
("How should you protect yourself from UV exposure when operating outdoors?",
 "Sunscreen, a hat and long sleeves", ["Only the shade of the overhead guard", "A tinted visor and short sleeves", "Hi-vis vest and no sunscreen"],
 "The overhead guard gives little real shade. Australian sun protection advice is to cover up, wear a hat and use sunscreen when working outdoors."),
("Why should you avoid driving a forklift over freshly backfilled ground?",
 "It may sink under the wheels", ["It scratches the tyre tread", "It confuses the reversing beeper", "It speeds up the hydraulics"],
 "Backfilled ground is not compacted and can give way under the concentrated weight of a loaded forklift, tipping it. Use another route or have the ground made suitable."),
("Your route crosses a steel trench cover. What should you check?",
 "That it is rated for the truck", ["That you cross it quickly", "That the load is carried up high", "That you cross at an angle"],
 "A trench cover or steel plate must be rated for the combined weight of the truck and load, and secured in place. If you cannot confirm it, find another route."),
("How should you cross railway tracks with a forklift?",
 "Slowly and at an angle", ["Quickly to bounce across", "With the load raised high", "Driving along the rails"],
 "Crossing slowly at an angle stops both wheels on one axle dropping against a rail at once. A raised load or speed makes the jolt far more dangerous."),
("There is a large pothole on your usual travel route. What should you do?",
 "Avoid it and report it", ["Speed up to roll over it", "Lift the load to clear it", "Drive through it in reverse"],
 "A wheel dropping into a pothole can jolt the truck and load and cause a tip. Go around it and report it so it can be repaired."),
("What is the main risk of driving a loaded forklift onto soft soil?",
 "A wheel sinks and it tips", ["The engine overheats", "The forks bend upward under load", "The horn stops working"],
 "Forklifts carry a lot of weight on small wheels, so soft ground can give way under one wheel and tip the truck. Check the surface suits the truck and task first."),
("A spotter is guiding you and you lose sight of them. What should you do?",
 "Stop straight away", ["Keep going slowly", "Sound the horn and continue", "Reverse to find them"],
 "If you cannot see your spotter or their signals, stop until contact is back. They may be in the path of the truck or the load."),
("When coordinating a lift by two-way radio, what is good practice?",
 "Repeat back each instruction", ["Talk while others transmit", "Keep the channel open always", "Skip names to save time"],
 "Repeating instructions back confirms they were heard correctly. Use agreed call signs and wait for a clear channel before speaking."),
("A supervisor's instruction for a lift is unclear to you. What should you do?",
 "Ask questions until it is clear", ["Go with your best guess", "Wait for the next shift", "Ask another operator to do it for you"],
 "Questioning is part of safe communication. Confirm the load, route and placement before starting rather than guessing."),
("You must move drums marked with a dangerous goods class label. What should you do first?",
 "Check the SDS and site procedure", ["Move them before others arrive", "Lift them higher for safety", "Double stack them to save on trips"],
 "Dangerous goods need specific handling, segregation and spill procedures. Read the safety data sheet and site procedure before moving them."),
("You must work in a narrow area with racking close on both sides. What helps most?",
 "Slow speed and a planned route", ["Faster turns to save time", "A higher fork travel height", "Driving with the mast tilted out"],
 "Restricted spaces raise the risk of striking racks, structures and people. Plan the route, go slowly and use a spotter if your view is limited."),
("What is the first step of a risk assessment for a forklift task?",
 "Identify the hazards", ["Choose the PPE", "Review the controls", "Rate the likelihood of harm"],
 "Risk management starts with identifying hazards, then assessing the risk, controlling it and reviewing the controls. PPE is the last step of the hierarchy, not the first."),
("A barrier listed in the traffic plan is missing from the work area. What should you do?",
 "Report it before starting work", ["Work around the gap very carefully", "Make your own sign for it", "Ignore it if it is quiet"],
 "Risk controls that are missing or deficient must be reported to the relevant person before work starts. Do not improvise or assume the area will stay quiet."),
("A sign at the warehouse entrance shows a 10 km/h speed limit. When does it apply to you?",
 "At all times in that area", ["Only when carrying a load", "Only when people are about", "Only on the night shift"],
 "Site speed limits apply whenever you drive in that area, loaded or not. You may need to go even slower for the conditions."),
("You are taking medicine that warns it may cause drowsiness. What should you do?",
 "Tell your supervisor first", ["Operate it, but drive more slowly", "Have a coffee and start", "Only lift light loads"],
 "Anything that affects alertness is a risk to you and others. Tell your supervisor before operating so they can decide on other duties."),
("Your phone rings while you are driving a forklift. What should you do?",
 "Stop the truck before answering", ["Answer it on straight aisles only", "Answer while reversing slowly", "Text back, but don't talk"],
 "Driving a forklift needs your full attention and both hands. Stop and park safely before using a phone or radio handset, or follow the site rule."),
("Before driving onto a trailer at a loading dock, what should you confirm?",
 "It is restrained and braked", ["The trailer driver is in the cab", "The dock door is half open", "Its engine is running"],
 "A trailer that creeps away from the dock can drop the forklift between the trailer and dock. Confirm the trailer is braked and restrained or chocked first."),
("A fire alarm sounds while you are carrying a load. What should you do?",
 "Lower the load, park and evacuate", ["Finish the lift first, then evacuate", "Drive the load to the exit", "Leave it raised and run"],
 "Lower the load, park the truck clear of exits and shut it down, then follow the site emergency procedure. A truck left at an exit or with a raised load blocks or endangers others."),
("What is a blue spot light projected on the floor ahead of a forklift for?",
 "Warning people a truck is near", ["Lighting up the load at height", "Showing the truck's load centre", "Marking the exclusion zone"],
 "The blue spot is a visual warning device that shows pedestrians a forklift is approaching, often before they can see it. It does not replace looking and slowing down."),
("The reversing beeper is working. Do you still need to look behind before reversing?",
 "Yes, always look where you travel", ["No, the beeper warns everyone behind", "Only on the night shift", "Only when carrying a load"],
 "Audible warnings support you but people may not hear them in a noisy area. Always look in the direction of travel."),
("Verbal instructions cannot be heard over machine noise. How should you communicate?",
 "Agreed hand signals or radio", ["Shout louder over the machine noise", "Sound the horn non-stop", "Flash the headlights twice"],
 "Use the communication method agreed for the task, such as standard hand signals or two-way radio. Agree the signals before the lift starts."),
("A task means working across a sloping yard. What should you check first?",
 "The maker's slope limits", ["Only the tyre pressure", "That the load is raised for clearance", "Only the fuel level"],
 "Slopes reduce stability, so check the manufacturer's limits and the risk assessment before working on one. Keep loads low and never travel across a steep slope."),
("Why is cracked or broken concrete a hazard for a forklift?",
 "Jolts can unsettle the load", ["It drains the hydraulic oil", "It upsets the reversing beeper", "It shortens the load centre"],
 "Small wheels and stiff tyres pass every bump to the truck and load, which can shift the load or tip the truck. Slow down, keep loads low and report damaged surfaces."),
("In an area with many pedestrians, what travel speed is right?",
 "Slow enough to stop safely", ["The truck's top speed", "Whatever keeps the job moving", "Fast, to cut exposure time"],
 "Your speed must let you stop in the distance you can see, especially where people may step out. Follow the posted limit and go slower if conditions need it."),
]
